1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,131
This is the AceVector (Snapdeal) I P O, a mainboard offer,

2
00:00:04,131 --> 00:00:08,405
open from the twenty-fifth to the twenty-ninth of September.

3
00:00:08,905 --> 00:00:11,432
The price band is ₹30 to ₹32.

4
00:00:11,432 --> 00:00:16,745
Every figure here comes from the final red herring prospectus

5
00:00:16,745 --> 00:00:18,575
and exchange notices;

6
00:00:18,575 --> 00:00:21,972
the final price is fixed after bidding,

7
00:00:21,972 --> 00:00:25,631
so valuations are computed at the ₹32 cap.

8
00:00:26,131 --> 00:00:27,368
First, the business.

9
00:00:27,868 --> 00:00:31,510
AceVector is the parent of Snapdeal,

10
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:37,883
a value-focused lifestyle marketplace that served 12.16 million

11
00:00:37,883 --> 00:00:39,703
customers in FY26,

12
00:00:39,703 --> 00:00:43,143
with 69.65% of them repeat buyers.

13
00:00:43,643 --> 00:00:45,475
It also owns Unicommerce,

14
00:00:45,475 --> 00:00:49,433
which sells e-commerce software to sellers and brands,

15
00:00:49,433 --> 00:00:52,219
and Stellaro, its consumer-brands arm.

16
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:54,319
The financial checkpoint.

17
00:00:54,819 --> 00:01:03,229
FY26 revenue was ₹510.38 Cr, up from ₹395.02 Cr.

18
00:01:03,229 --> 00:01:10,413
The company made a net loss of ₹45.51 Cr.

19
00:01:10,913 --> 00:01:12,535
The trend is improving.

20
00:01:13,035 --> 00:01:21,089
The loss narrowed from ₹126.31 Cr to ₹45.51 Cr as revenue grew 29.20%.

21
00:01:21,089 --> 00:01:24,540
But until it reports a profit,

22
00:01:24,540 --> 00:01:30,293
there is no earnings multiple to anchor the price.

23
00:01:30,793 --> 00:01:34,868
The offer size at the cap is ₹420.00 Cr.

24
00:01:35,368 --> 00:01:40,405
₹287.00 Cr is fresh issue that goes into the company,

25
00:01:40,405 --> 00:01:47,059
and ₹133.00 Cr is an offer for sale that goes to selling shareholders.

26
00:01:47,559 --> 00:01:51,791
So 68.33% of the deal is new capital,

27
00:01:51,791 --> 00:01:56,711
and 31.67% is an exit for existing holders.

28
00:01:57,211 --> 00:01:58,533
Where does the money go?

29
00:01:59,033 --> 00:02:02,042
Of the ₹287.00 Cr fresh issue,

30
00:02:02,042 --> 00:02:07,659
₹132.00 Cr goes to marketing and ₹50.00 Cr to technology

31
00:02:07,659 --> 00:02:10,468
infrastructure for Snapdeal.

32
00:02:10,968 --> 00:02:14,936
The rest can fund acquisitions and general corporate purposes.

33
00:02:15,436 --> 00:02:20,757
Existing shareholders sell 4,15,62,500 shares,

34
00:02:20,757 --> 00:02:26,657
worth ₹133.00 Cr at the cap, in the offer for sale.

35
00:02:27,157 --> 00:02:28,160
Valuation.

36
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:31,583
AceVector made a loss, so it has no P E.

37
00:02:32,083 --> 00:02:33,784
Of its RHP peers,

38
00:02:33,784 --> 00:02:38,787
FirstCry's parent and Meesho are also loss-making,

39
00:02:38,787 --> 00:02:43,389
and Nykaa's parent trades at 462.50x earnings.

40
00:02:43,889 --> 00:02:48,171
So judge this one on the path to profit and on revenue growth,

41
00:02:48,171 --> 00:02:49,415
not on a multiple.

42
00:02:49,915 --> 00:02:51,408
Now balance the evidence.

43
00:02:51,908 --> 00:02:53,418
Watch-out:

44
00:02:53,418 --> 00:02:56,137
Still loss-making:

45
00:02:56,137 --> 00:02:59,158
₹45.51 Cr FY26 loss.

46
00:02:59,158 --> 00:03:00,518
Strength:

47
00:03:00,518 --> 00:03:05,049
Loss narrowed from ₹126.31 Cr.

48
00:03:05,549 --> 00:03:06,900
Watch-out:

49
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:11,896
Proceeds mostly fund marketing spend.

50
00:03:11,896 --> 00:03:13,111
Strength:

51
00:03:13,111 --> 00:03:17,432
Revenue up 29.20% to ₹510.38 Cr.

52
00:03:17,932 --> 00:03:19,067
Watch-out:

53
00:03:19,067 --> 00:03:22,358
Negative return on net worth:

54
00:03:22,358 --> 00:03:23,266
-59.54%.

55
00:03:23,266 --> 00:03:24,287
Strength:

56
00:03:24,287 --> 00:03:25,649
Diversified:

57
00:03:25,649 --> 00:03:28,940
marketplace, SaaS and brands.

58
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,571
How to apply.

59
00:03:31,071 --> 00:03:36,027
The minimum bid is one lot of 468 shares,

60
00:03:36,027 --> 00:03:39,412
which is ₹14,976 at the cap.

61
00:03:39,912 --> 00:03:43,387
Retail investors can bid up to two lakh rupees,

62
00:03:43,387 --> 00:03:47,528
and allotment is by lottery if retail is oversubscribed.

63
00:03:48,028 --> 00:03:52,571
Check live subscription on the N S E or B S E website,

64
00:03:52,571 --> 00:03:54,001
not social media.

65
00:03:54,501 --> 00:03:55,461
Let's recap.

66
00:03:55,961 --> 00:04:03,017
FY26 revenue ₹510.38 Cr, with a net loss of ₹45.51 Cr.

67
00:04:03,017 --> 00:04:11,248
The offer is ₹420.00 Cr, of which ₹133.00 Cr is offer for sale.

68
00:04:11,248 --> 00:04:15,690
There is no P/E because of losses.

69
00:04:15,690 --> 00:04:20,132
The minimum investment is ₹14,976.

70
00:04:20,632 --> 00:04:24,806
This video is public-source education from the red herring

71
00:04:24,806 --> 00:04:27,108
prospectus and exchange notices.

72
00:04:27,108 --> 00:04:31,066
It is not investment advice and not a buy or sell call.

73
00:04:31,066 --> 00:04:32,865
Read the final documents,

74
00:04:32,865 --> 00:04:35,744
check live subscription on the exchange,

75
00:04:35,744 --> 00:04:38,478
and consult a SEBI-registered adviser.

76
00:04:38,478 --> 00:04:39,917
Thanks for watching.

